{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Nano LLM From Scratch\n",
    "\n",
    "**Goal:** Train a tiny autoregressive transformer from scratch to generate Shakespearean text. We will implement the causal self-attention mechanism, the Feed-Forward Network (FFN), and the full Transformer Block strictly in PyTorch.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Prerequisites:** You must have a basic understanding of `torch.nn.Module`, tensor reshaping (`.view()`), and matrix multiplication (`@`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "import torch.nn.functional as F\n",
    "import urllib.request\n",
    "import math\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set random seed for reproducibility\n",
    "torch.manual_seed(1337)\n",
    "device = 'mps' if torch.backends.mps.is_available() else 'cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu'\n",
    "print(f\"Using device: {device}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. The Data: Shakespeare\n",
    "We will download the 'tinyshakespeare' dataset. It is a 1MB file containing a compilation of Shakespeare's works."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/karpathy/char-rnn/master/data/tinyshakespeare/input.txt\"\n",
    "text = urllib.request.urlopen(url).read().decode('utf-8')\n",
    "print(f\"Length of dataset in characters: {len(text):,}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "chars = sorted(list(set(text)))\n",
    "vocab_size = len(chars)\n",
    "print(f\"Vocabulary size: {vocab_size} unique characters\")\n",
    "print(f\"Vocabulary: {''.join(chars)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Tokenization\n",
    "Instead of using a complex BPE tokenizer like modern LLMs, we will use a simple character-level tokenizer. Each unique character gets mapped to an integer."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "stoi = { ch:i for i,ch in enumerate(chars) }\n",
    "itos = { i:ch for i,ch in enumerate(chars) }\n",
    "encode = lambda s: [stoi[c] for c in s] # encoder: string -> list of integers\n",
    "decode = lambda l: ''.join([itos[i] for i in l]) # decoder: list of integers -> string\n",
    "\n",
    "data = torch.tensor(encode(text), dtype=torch.long)\n",
    "print(f\"Encoded data shape: {data.shape}, dtype: {data.dtype}\")\n",
    "print(f\"First 20 tokens: {data[:20]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Train/Val Split and Batch Generation\n",
    "We need to feed the model batches of data. If our context length (block_size) is $T$, the model looks at tokens $x_0 \\dots x_{T-1}$ and tries to predict $x_1 \\dots x_T$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "n = int(0.9 * len(data)) # 90% train, 10% val\n",
    "train_data = data[:n]\n",
    "val_data = data[n:]\n",
    "\n",
    "block_size = 64 # Context length (T)\n",
    "batch_size = 32 # Number of independent sequences to process in parallel (B)\n",
    "\n",
    "def get_batch(split):\n",
    "    data_split = train_data if split == 'train' else val_data\n",
    "    ix = torch.randint(len(data_split) - block_size, (batch_size,))\n",
    "    x = torch.stack([data_split[i:i+block_size] for i in ix])\n",
    "    y = torch.stack([data_split[i+1:i+block_size+1] for i in ix])\n",
    "    return x.to(device), y.to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "xb, yb = get_batch('train')\n",
    "print(f\"Input batch shape (B, T): {xb.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Target batch shape (B, T): {yb.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. The Model Architecture\n",
    "Now we build the Transformer. We will implement it layer by layer."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Exercise 1: Causal Self-Attention\n",
    "Implement the single-head attention mechanism. \n",
    "Given an input $x \in \\mathbb{R}^{B \\times T \\times C}$ (where $C$ is `d_model` or `n_embd`):\n",
    "1. Project $x$ into Queries ($Q$), Keys ($K$), and Values ($V$).\n",
    "2. Compute the attention scores: $S = \\frac{Q K^T}{\\sqrt{d_k}}$.\n",
    "3. Apply a causal mask (lower triangular matrix of 1s, upper triangular is $-\\infty$) so tokens cannot look into the future.\n",
    "4. Apply Softmax to get probabilities.\n",
    "5. Multiply by $V$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class Head(nn.Module):\n",
    "    \"\"\" One head of self-attention \"\"\"\n",
    "    def __init__(self, head_size):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        # TODO: Define nn.Linear layers for key, query, and value (bias=False)\n",
    "        self.key = None \n",
    "        self.query = None\n",
    "        self.value = None\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Register a lower-triangular mask in the module state (not a parameter)\n",
    "        self.register_buffer('tril', torch.tril(torch.ones(block_size, block_size)))\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, x):\n",
    "        B, T, C = x.shape\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # TODO: Compute k, q, v (Shape: B, T, head_size)\n",
    "        k = None\n",
    "        q = None\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # TODO: Compute attention scores (wei). \n",
    "        # Be careful with the transpose! You want to multiply (B, T, head_size) @ (B, head_size, T)\n",
    "        wei = None\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Apply causal mask\n",
    "        wei = wei.masked_fill(self.tril[:T, :T] == 0, float('-inf'))\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # TODO: Apply Softmax (dim=-1)\n",
    "        wei = None\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # TODO: Multiply weights by Values (v)\n",
    "        v = None\n",
    "        out = None\n",
    "        \n",
    "        return out"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Multi-Head Attention\n",
    "We run several heads in parallel and concatenate their results."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class MultiHeadAttention(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, num_heads, head_size):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.heads = nn.ModuleList([Head(head_size) for _ in range(num_heads)])\n",
    "        self.proj = nn.Linear(num_heads * head_size, n_embd)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, x):\n",
    "        out = torch.cat([h(x) for h in self.heads], dim=-1)\n",
    "        out = self.proj(out)\n",
    "        return out"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Exercise 2: Feed Forward Network\n",
    "After attention, the model needs to think about the aggregated information. We use a simple 2-layer MLP with a ReLU activation. Note that the inner dimension is typically 4x the embedding dimension."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class FeedForward(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, n_embd):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        # TODO: Define a Sequential block:\n",
    "        # 1. Linear(n_embd, 4 * n_embd)\n",
    "        # 2. ReLU()\n",
    "        # 3. Linear(4 * n_embd, n_embd)\n",
    "        self.net = None\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, x):\n",
    "        return self.net(x)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Exercise 3: The Transformer Block (Pre-LN)\n",
    "Combine the Multi-Head Attention and the Feed Forward Network. \n",
    "Crucially, implement the **Pre-LN Architecture** with residual connections:\n",
    "$x = x + \\text{Attention}(\\text{LayerNorm}(x))$\n",
    "$x = x + \\text{FFN}(\\text{LayerNorm}(x))$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class Block(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, n_embd, n_head):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        head_size = n_embd // n_head\n",
    "        self.sa = MultiHeadAttention(n_head, head_size)\n",
    "        self.ffwd = FeedForward(n_embd)\n",
    "        self.ln1 = nn.LayerNorm(n_embd)\n",
    "        self.ln2 = nn.LayerNorm(n_embd)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, x):\n",
    "        # TODO: Implement the Pre-LN residual connections\n",
    "        # 1. Apply ln1 to x, pass it to self.sa, add the result back to x\n",
    "        # 2. Apply ln2 to the new x, pass it to self.ffwd, add the result back to x\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "        return x"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### The Final Model Assembly\n",
    "We combine token embeddings, positional embeddings (simple learned vectors for now, not RoPE), the transformer blocks, and the final linear projection to the vocabulary."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "n_embd = 128\n",
    "n_head = 4\n",
    "n_layer = 3\n",
    "\n",
    "class NanoGPT(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.token_embedding_table = nn.Embedding(vocab_size, n_embd)\n",
    "        self.position_embedding_table = nn.Embedding(block_size, n_embd)\n",
    "        self.blocks = nn.Sequential(*[Block(n_embd, n_head=n_head) for _ in range(n_layer)])\n",
    "        self.ln_f = nn.LayerNorm(n_embd) # final layer norm\n",
    "        self.lm_head = nn.Linear(n_embd, vocab_size)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, idx, targets=None):\n",
    "        B, T = idx.shape\n",
    "        \n",
    "        tok_emb = self.token_embedding_table(idx) # (B,T,C)\n",
    "        pos_emb = self.position_embedding_table(torch.arange(T, device=device)) # (T,C)\n",
    "        x = tok_emb + pos_emb # (B,T,C)\n",
    "        x = self.blocks(x) # (B,T,C)\n",
    "        x = self.ln_f(x) # (B,T,C)\n",
    "        logits = self.lm_head(x) # (B,T,vocab_size)\n",
    "\n",
    "        if targets is None:\n",
    "            loss = None\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            B, T, C = logits.shape\n",
    "            logits = logits.view(B*T, C)\n",
    "            targets = targets.view(B*T)\n",
    "            loss = F.cross_entropy(logits, targets)\n",
    "\n",
    "        return logits, loss\n",
    "\n",
    "    def generate(self, idx, max_new_tokens):\n",
    "        # idx is (B, T) array of indices in the current context\n",
    "        for _ in range(max_new_tokens):\n",
    "            # crop idx to the last block_size tokens\n",
    "            idx_cond = idx[:, -block_size:]\n",
    "            # get the predictions\n",
    "            logits, loss = self(idx_cond)\n",
    "            # focus only on the last time step\n",
    "            logits = logits[:, -1, :] # becomes (B, C)\n",
    "            # apply softmax to get probabilities\n",
    "            probs = F.softmax(logits, dim=-1) # (B, C)\n",
    "            # sample from the distribution\n",
    "            idx_next = torch.multinomial(probs, num_samples=1) # (B, 1)\n",
    "            # append sampled index to the running sequence\n",
    "            idx = torch.cat((idx, idx_next), dim=1) # (B, T+1)\n",
    "        return idx\n",
    "\n",
    "model = NanoGPT().to(device)\n",
    "print(f\"Model parameters: {sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())/1e6:.2f} M\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. The Training Loop\n",
    "We use the AdamW optimizer. (If you want to feel the power, run this on an Apple Silicon Mac using the `mps` device!)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=1e-3)\n",
    "max_iters = 3000\n",
    "eval_interval = 300\n",
    "\n",
    "@torch.no_grad()\n",
    "def estimate_loss():\n",
    "    out = {}\n",
    "    model.eval()\n",
    "    for split in ['train', 'val']:\n",
    "        losses = torch.zeros(100)\n",
    "        for k in range(100):\n",
    "            X, Y = get_batch(split)\n",
    "            logits, loss = model(X, Y)\n",
    "            losses[k] = loss.item()\n",
    "        out[split] = losses.mean()\n",
    "    model.train()\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "for iter in range(max_iters):\n",
    "    if iter % eval_interval == 0:\n",
    "        losses = estimate_loss()\n",
    "        print(f\"step {iter}: train loss {losses['train']:.4f}, val loss {losses['val']:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    xb, yb = get_batch('train')\n",
    "\n",
    "    logits, loss = model(xb, yb)\n",
    "    optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n",
    "    loss.backward()\n",
    "    optimizer.step()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Inference\n",
    "Let's see what Shakespearean text our tiny model generates!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "context = torch.zeros((1, 1), dtype=torch.long, device=device)\n",
    "print(decode(model.generate(context, max_new_tokens=500)[0].tolist()))"
   ]
  }
